t launches the opponent in the  air  normally a useful move for starting  comes already but it will become a  lethal hit if you activate a soul charge  sometime during the previous round  maybe one of the most unique lethal hit  conditions is ivy's down forward k  which is a lethal hit versus only male  characters  it's important to mention that you  shouldn't have to feel obligated to  learn every single legal hit for your  character  and especially not every single legal  hit in the game there's just way too  many  instead you should focus on ones that  seem practical for your gameplay  exactly like for calyx's example he's  got this low attack on the fourth hit  it's going to act to be a lethal so this  might be a good low attack  for you to look for also if you have  some other legally conditions to look  for you might want to look for stuff  that's like  legal hits on a whipped attack or lethal  hits on a guard impact here  these kind of things are going to be the  ones that are most useful to find an  actual matchup  the rest of you can kind of figure out  over time as you have more experience  that'll do it for this episode this  tutorial was made in partnership with  the playstation competition center team  you can sign up for their open series  competitions on compete.playstation.com  subscribe to the bne esports channel for  more tutorials and soul calibur 6  content

